# Line endings are decided here, not by each clone's configuration.
#
# Measured on 2026-10-13: adding this file at all switched on the CRLF conversion that
# `core.autocrlf=true` asks for, and `skillflow-prompts schemas --check` compares bytes.
# A fresh checkout then carried one extra carriage return in each generated schema, the
# check called them stale, and the Windows build went red on a commit whose working tree
# was clean. Pinning the working-tree ending removes the difference between two clones.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary

# The decorative images stay in the repository and out of the archive.
#
# `git archive` builds the zip people attach to a conversation. Four megabytes of
# decoration in it would be paid by every person who uploads it, for pictures that carry no
# information. On GitHub the images show normally; in the zip the README links simply find
# no file.
docs/images/ export-ignore
